**Definition 6.4 (native consumer specification).** A
complete realization must supply one fixed finite PR57 graph
$G$ for boundary-stopped replay, prefix selection, framing, publication,
Call and return, together with the following commuting relation:

$$
\operatorname{decode}(\operatorname{Run}_G(B_s,U(k)))
       =(s[0:k],X(s[0:k]))
\quad(a\le k\le b).
\tag{RCA.7}
$$

The graph must read only actual acquired material at admitted owner-local
entry states. Its realized virtual state must include the full original
cell/receipt/code/permission carrier. Every simulated primitive requires
a finite paid representation update, and output requires actual allocated
backing. A mathematical state-transition function, a Partrec code-existence
theorem or an abstract Native localStep is not this graph.

The finite-string computation of Theorem 4.4 and the native enumerator of
Theorem 5.7 alone do not supply $G$. Sections 11–16 specify its finite
compilation, actual row simulator, admission and return, and paid late
installation. Propositions 6.2 and 6.3 are reused after materialization;
they are not substitutes for that construction.

